<title>POLAND: Poles to gain access to OECD securities in January.</title>
<headline>Poles to gain access to OECD securities in January.</headline>
<byline>Jacek Ramotowski</byline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new foreign exchange regulation, which will allow Poles to invest in stocks and debt securities issued in OECD countries, should come into force by the end of this month, a finance ministry official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The new regulation has been cleared and it allows Polish residents and institutions to buy securities (from OECD countries) through those domestic securities houses which will receive relevant licences,&quot; Malgorzata Wesolowska, of the ministry's foreign exchange policy department, told Reuters.</p>
</text>
